within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01F_MonoclonalAntibodiesAndAntibodyDrugConjugates.L01FA01_Rituximab;
model Rituximab_Li2024_PD_cd19_b_cell
  "indirect_response_ii exposure-response sweep — Li_2024 :: CD19+ B-cell (CD19+ B-cell)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.IndirectTurnoverSweep(
    E0 = 591.428571429,      // [/μL]
    Emax = 389.7,  // type IV effect term
    EC50 = 1.31e-06,  // [kg; mg × 1e-06]
    gamma = 6.65,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 mg per second
  // e0_from_kin_kout: no baseline row; E0 = kin/kout (4.14/0.007 = 591.4) — the paper's stated baseline may differ
  // emax_not_a_fraction: type II needs Imax ≤ 1 but the record has 389.7; bound as the reciprocal stimulation form (IV) the paper fitted
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 5.4, Interval = 0.0108),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Rituximab_Li2024_PD_cd19_b_cell</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Li Z et al., <i>Frontiers in pharmacology 15:1526936</i> 2024 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphar.2024.1526936\">doi:10.3389/fphar.2024.1526936</a>) — CD19+ B-cell [/μL] against rituximab mg — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_ii.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    = 591.428571429 /μL      drug-free response (baseline) (kin/kout, Q327/Q328)
  Emax  =      389.7          maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =       1.31 mg       exposure at half of the maximal effect term (ED50, Q322)
  gamma =       6.65          Hill coefficient (γ, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.IndirectTurnoverSweep\">IndirectTurnoverSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg of rituximab per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><p>The effect term enters as a reciprocal (steady state of <code>der(R) = Kin - Kout*(1 + Emax*frac)*R</code>), so EC50 is the exposure at half the maximal STIMULATION of turnover, not at half the response.</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 591.4   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (1.31 mg)  response 3.02
  exposure -> infinity  response 1.514</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Li_2024: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Rituximab_Li2024_PD_cd19_b_cell;
